A||||1||Cheever2||Cost for frame shop to straighten front corner? ||||5||
Z||000000||Cheever2||01-15-2001||08:01 PM||||Does anybody knows what frame shops charge?  All the talk about headlight customizing became a non-issue when I put the hood back on and found it overlapped the fender at the doorpost by at least one inch.  Since the metal has to be straightened for that, I will have them ensure the headlights can move up & down again.<BR>I have a frame shop just up the road, but wondering what to expect for pulling a corner out.  Don't wanna faint on the shop floor, rather do it here sitting down.<BR> <P>------------------<BR><I>Chuck Hodges</I>||||reg||5
Z||000001||rogergarrison||01-15-2001||08:08 PM||||my frame shop charges me $100 set up charge and $50 for each pull they make. Most drivable damage can be straighted with one pull. Thats my shop price. They may charge more or even give you a break. Youll save if you do things for them ahead of time,  like pull off the fender, hood, bumper, etc.They pull it and measure frame points, so its not necessary for you to give them the new parts, but they may like them to double check.<BR>||||reg||1
